      "id": "claim_60d0aea2e79743bb850eb903cef4eb15",
      "statement": "Settings.from_env loads a .env file at most once per process, probing the current working directory first and then the repository root, stopping at the first file found and loading it with override=False so real environment variables take precedence over file values.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://pipeline/core/config.py#L20-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bb66051990aba49d396e6613baf8be539832b48ee6eed0e2f73b99c8b8d3835a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a03c7c12db8048698fb81715425555cd",
      "statement": "The _env helper treats an empty-string environment variable identically to an unset one and returns the dataclass default, so a blank assignment such as TRINO_HOST= behaves as an omitted setting rather than configuring an empty value.",
